# Round-2 stats audit — statistical validity

Role: statistical validity. Round-1 work (numbers/integrity/claims/repro) is not repeated; already-known issues (sigma-division, rerank overgeneralization, +10.35 RealTalk-only, hardcoded paths, LoCoMo 1531-vs-1535) are not re-reported as new, but are referenced where they condition a statistical claim.

## 1. VERDICT (3 lines)

STOP survives this audit: correction kills every pro-code "SIG" while the anti-code gaps are an order of magnitude larger than any noise scale I can construct. But the four headline numbers (-7.80, +10, -2.27, r=-0.78) were all published without the inference that justifies them, and for two headline claims the per-question data needed to compute a valid interval was never stored. Two CRITICAL findings (both missing-CI/missing-data, neither reversing STOP).

## 2. Findings summary

| ID | Severity | Bottom line |
|----|----|----|
| S1 | CRITICAL | T1 gaps: no CI, paired data discarded |
| S2 | CRITICAL | Ladder/sign+10: no CI, no per-query store |
| S3 | HIGH | ITQ-worse-than-random dies under correction |
| S4 | HIGH | LoCoMo +1.07 borderline; story problem |
| S5 | HIGH | No held-out set; all selection on test |
